"icon:lock[title=Fixed at build time] [[quarkus-smallrye-graphql_quarkus-smallrye-graphql-authorization-client-init-payload-name]] [.property-path]##link:#quarkus-smallrye-graphql_quarkus-smallrye-graphql-authorization-client-init-payload-name[`+++quarkus.smallrye-graphql.authorization-client-init-payload-name+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.smallrye-graphql.authorization-client-init-payload-name+++[]\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"The name of the key inside the client init payload which contains Authorization information. The associated value of this is treated in the same way as sent over as a Authorization header. Using headers is the preferred way, however in some languages, such as JavaScript, it is not possible to send headers over websockets.  +\n"
"If sending headers are not an option, another viable option is link:https://quarkus.io/guides/websockets-next-reference#bearer-token-authentication[Bearer Token Authentication] which might be preferable over this in some cases as it's able to inject headers before the WebSocket is opened.  +\n"
"Default is undefined, which means the client init payload will not be checked for Authorization information.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_SMALLRYE_GRAPHQL_AUTHORIZATION_CLIENT_INIT_PAYLOAD_NAME+++[]\n"
"--"
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"icon:lock[title=Fixed at build time] [[quarkus-smallrye-graphql_quarkus-smallrye-graphql-authorization-client-init-payload-name]] [.property-path]##link:#quarkus-smallrye-graphql_quarkus-smallrye-graphql-authorization-client-init-payload-name[`+++quarkus.smallrye-graphql.authorization-client-init-payload-name+++`]##\n"
"config_property_copy_button:+++quarkus.smallrye-graphql.authorization-client-init-payload-name+++[]"
msgstr "[lock]  link:#quarkus-smallrye-graphql_quarkus-smallrye-graphql-authorization-client-init-payload-name[quarkus.smallrye-graphql.authorization-client-init-payload-name] config_property_copy_button:quarkus.smallrye-graphql.authorization-client-init-payload-name[]"

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The name of the key inside the client init payload which contains Authorization information. The associated value of this is treated in the same way as sent over as a Authorization header. Using headers is the preferred way, however in some languages, such as JavaScript, it is not possible to send headers over websockets.  +\n"
"If sending headers are not an option, another viable option is link:https://quarkus.io/guides/websockets-next-reference#bearer-token-authentication[Bearer Token Authentication] which might be preferable over this in some cases as it's able to inject headers before the WebSocket is opened.  +\n"
"Default is undefined, which means the client init payload will not be checked for Authorization information."
msgstr ""
"O nome da chave dentro da carga de inicialização do cliente que contém as informações de autorização. O valor associado a ela é tratado da mesma forma que se fosse enviado como um cabeçalho de autorização. O uso de cabeçalhos é a forma preferida; no entanto, em algumas linguagens, como o JavaScript, não é possível enviar cabeçalhos por meio de WebSockets.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"Caso o envio de cabeçalhos não seja uma opção, outra alternativa viável é link:https://quarkus.io/guides/websockets-next-reference#bearer-token-authentication[a autenticação por token Bearer] , que pode ser preferível a esta opção em alguns casos, pois permite inserir cabeçalhos antes da abertura do WebSocket.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"O padrão é indefinido, o que significa que a carga de inicialização do cliente não será verificada quanto às informações de autorização."

